  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "masu-stem + tsutsu\n食べつつ",
      "html": "masu-stem + tsutsu<br/>食べつつ",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "cfcd0ba76e1e3aa93365466791dbcb56b2b8f4a2a837be134198a2c80cd12e47",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "〜つつ(1)\n「Ａつつ、Ｂ」: A and B are done simultaneously.\n＊This expression is more \"solid\" than ながら. See examples #6213, #6214, and #6215.\nFORMATION:\nＶ(minus ます) + つつ\n\n〜つつ(2)・つつも\n＊This expression is used alongside negative emotions. The forms used most often include: 「〜と思いつつ」 and 「〜と知りつつ」. See examples #6216, #6217, and #6218.\nFORMATION:\nＶ(minus ます) + つつ・つつも",
      "html": "〜つつ(1)<br/>「Ａつつ、Ｂ」: A and B are done simultaneously.<br/>＊This expression is more \"solid\" than ながら. See examples #6213, #6214, and #6215.<br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(minus ます) + つつ<br/><br/>〜つつ(2)・つつも<br/>＊This expression is used alongside negative emotions. The forms used most often include: 「〜と思いつつ」 and 「〜と知りつつ」. See examples #6216, #6217, and #6218.<br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(minus ます) + つつ・つつも",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "43ae3bb18735f3ea721cdef5e5fe892cb6a4f506d12fb7ee6d3370f677eba631",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Pls see also 〜ながら",
      "html": "Pls see also 〜ながら",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "880faccae3f2bfda8ea15e272cbadb31cf7144dd4a8f804b74cfb2e8b33d73ac",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Is 何々つつ　mostly a written expression? People look at me funny when I talk like a book, so I'd like to clear that up.\n\nAny chance of tagging the expressions on jGram as being either mainly written or spoken?",
      "html": "Is 何々つつ　mostly a written expression? People look at me funny when I talk like a book, so I'd like to clear that up.<br/><br/>Any chance of tagging the expressions on jGram as being either mainly written or spoken?",
      "credits_raw": "Leslie",
      "content_sha256": "d8ecdc44dccdec35a41fc3d72479556515190b9fb5e7cc84bbd6c51364f7555b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Formed from Verb -masu base + tsutsu\n\nVm = Verb -masu base",
      "html": "Formed from Verb -masu base + tsutsu<br/><br/>Vm = Verb -masu base",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "c56142f58d42d9cf44689009905f1a9b26120f10b55453b7ab301a0aeddcf05a",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "tagging written/spoken should be there, you're right. Also, degree of formailty (t-shirt or tie icon?).\n\nIt could be added to the notes section as a text note, though it would be nice to have a popup menu i guess... means more work for people entering stuff though.",
      "html": "tagging written/spoken should be there, you're right. Also, degree of formailty (t-shirt or tie icon?).<br/><br/>It could be added to the notes section as a text note, though it would be nice to have a popup menu i guess... means more work for people entering stuff though.",
